WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.523 --> 00:00:01.768
- [Instructor] Hi, and welcome back.

2
00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:03.588
In this section, we're
going to look at Git.

3
00:00:03.588 --> 00:00:06.966
And the first thing we
have to do is download Git.

4
00:00:06.966 --> 00:00:08.632
To download Git for Mac,

5
00:00:08.632 --> 00:00:13.261
just go to git-scm.com/download/mac,

6
00:00:13.261 --> 00:00:14.959
and that will begin the download,

7
00:00:14.959 --> 00:00:17.833
and you can instal it like
any other normal programme,

8
00:00:17.833 --> 00:00:22.073
and then it will be
accessible via your Terminal.

9
00:00:22.073 --> 00:00:26.201
There are also many
graphical interfaces for Git,

10
00:00:26.201 --> 00:00:27.228
and towards the end

11
00:00:27.228 --> 00:00:29.370
I will be recommending
one of them as well,

12
00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:32.035
but I think it's important
to start with the Terminal,

13
00:00:32.035 --> 00:00:36.806
so that we know how Git really
works behind the scenes.

14
00:00:36.806 --> 00:00:38.117
If you're on Windows,

15
00:00:38.117 --> 00:00:41.617
then go to git-for-windows.github.io,

16
00:00:42.705 --> 00:00:46.038
and download the Git Windows thing here.

17
00:00:47.668 --> 00:00:51.247
This provides a terminal
that lets you run Git,

18
00:00:51.247 --> 00:00:53.554
and also a number of other commands

19
00:00:53.554 --> 00:00:56.680
that are normally not present in Windows.

20
00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:58.204
So download that.

21
00:00:58.204 --> 00:00:59.467
And let's look at how you would

22
00:00:59.467 --> 00:01:02.300
download and instal this Git SCM.

23
00:01:03.272 --> 00:01:05.910
So I'm going to go over to my virtual box,

24
00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:08.470
and just to guide you through it.

25
00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:09.637
If you're using a Mac, by the way,

26
00:01:09.637 --> 00:01:11.500
you can just skip to the end.

27
00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.912
If you're using Windows,
you may want to stay.

28
00:01:13.912 --> 00:01:15.427
So launch Chrome,

29
00:01:15.427 --> 00:01:18.897
go to git-for-windows.github.io,

30
00:01:18.897 --> 00:01:20.397
and download that.

31
00:01:21.779 --> 00:01:23.807
And then that would
start the download there.

32
00:01:23.807 --> 00:01:26.474
I'm just going to speed through.

33
00:01:34.935 --> 00:01:38.518
Once that's done, just press it to instal.

34
00:01:42.267 --> 00:01:43.991
And then you can press Next.

35
00:01:43.991 --> 00:01:46.952
And here, this is an important thing,

36
00:01:46.952 --> 00:01:48.452
make sure to press

37
00:01:49.446 --> 00:01:53.529
this Associate .sh files
to be run with Bash.

38
00:01:54.775 --> 00:01:57.474
The other stuff, I would
also leave pressed,

39
00:01:57.474 --> 00:02:00.426
and you may even want to get
their icon on the desktop

40
00:02:00.426 --> 00:02:01.259
as well.

41
00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:09.142
And then I would leave the
first option pressed here,

42
00:02:09.142 --> 00:02:12.120
Use Git from Git Bash only.

43
00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:15.115
You can, if you want, use this one,

44
00:02:15.115 --> 00:02:17.388
Use Git from the Windows Command Prompt,

45
00:02:17.388 --> 00:02:19.426
but I would recommend the first one.

46
00:02:19.426 --> 00:02:21.028
If you use the second
one, then you can use

47
00:02:21.028 --> 00:02:24.511
the default Windows
Command Prompt to run Git,

48
00:02:24.511 --> 00:02:27.759
but the Windows Command
Prompt is lacking a few things

49
00:02:27.759 --> 00:02:30.310
that you would want from your terminal,

50
00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:32.077
so I would recommend always using

51
00:02:32.077 --> 00:02:33.976
the programme that this is installing,

52
00:02:33.976 --> 00:02:37.059
and leaving the option as number one.

53
00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:42.558
And finally, I would also leave
the first one pressed here.

54
00:02:47.746 --> 00:02:50.428
And I would also leave the
first one pressed here.

55
00:02:50.428 --> 00:02:54.799
This is just which sort
of console it's using.

56
00:02:54.799 --> 00:02:56.882
Leave that pressed there.

57
00:02:58.386 --> 00:03:00.955
And finally, these two you
can leave pressed if you want.

58
00:03:00.955 --> 00:03:01.788
They're not really going to make

59
00:03:01.788 --> 00:03:04.121
much of a difference for us.

60
00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:18.222
When that's done, you can
uncheck View Release Notes,

61
00:03:18.222 --> 00:03:20.389
and check Launch Git Bash.

62
00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:26.067
And that brings you to
this nice-looking terminal.

63
00:03:26.067 --> 00:03:30.648
It's trying to log in right
now as your Windows user.

64
00:03:30.648 --> 00:03:33.199
And my Windows computer is very slow.

65
00:03:33.199 --> 00:03:35.524
Yours will be a bit faster.

66
00:03:35.524 --> 00:03:36.569
And there you are.

67
00:03:36.569 --> 00:03:40.356
You have, essentially
what we've got on the Mac.

68
00:03:40.356 --> 00:03:42.707
Many of the things that we do on Mac

69
00:03:42.707 --> 00:03:44.632
work on this terminal,

70
00:03:44.632 --> 00:03:46.965
but they won't work on the

71
00:03:49.637 --> 00:03:51.536
Windows command line.

72
00:03:51.536 --> 00:03:53.652
So make sure to use this terminal

73
00:03:53.652 --> 00:03:57.587
whenever you are interacting with Git.

74
00:03:57.587 --> 00:03:58.420
And that's it.

75
00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:01.828
Now you can continue, and follow
the videos along as usual.

76
00:04:01.828 --> 00:04:04.275
And don't worry that we're
using Mac on the videos.

77
00:04:04.275 --> 00:04:08.515
All of the commands
work the same way here.

78
00:04:08.515 --> 00:04:09.456
So that's it.

79
00:04:09.456 --> 00:04:12.211
Thanks for watching, and I'll
see you on the next video.

